    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass \u2014 this repo's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to the new spec.\n\n**New identity key** \u2014 `IdentityKeys.java` now computes `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`, replacing the old human-readable `telephone|email|householdId` form. `forFields(...)` now takes `lastName` instead of `householdId`.\n\n**New `Soundex.java`** \u2014 a standard American Soundex encoder (letter + 3 digits), shared by both the identity key and the soft-match so they stay in agreement.\n\n**Duplicate detection (409)** \u2014 `RequireUniqueIdentity.java` now compares the single SHA-256 identity key against non-deleted owners. The email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `RequireOwnerFields`, a 400, upstream in the pipeline) and soft-deleted owners are still ignored. Because telephone is now part of the key, two owners with the same last name + postcode but different telephones no longer collide here \u2014 the separate `householdId`-based 409 is gone.\n\n**Soft match** \u2014 `AssignPossibleDuplicate.java` now flags a possible duplicate when `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match an existing non-deleted owner but the `identityKey` differs (so those different-telephone household members become soft matches rather than rejects).\n\n**Supporting** \u2014 `DuplicateIdentityException` message now references the identity key; javadoc in `AssignHousehold` corrected. `householdId` is still assigned (it still drives `householdSize`), just no longer used for duplicate detection.\n\nI kept the `sharesHousehold` declared-member bypass in both guards, since the spec only removed the `householdId`-derived 409 and didn't call for dropping that escape hatch.",
